{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FULL RETRACTION (supersedes both prior entries on this topic). My claim that 'landing a change invalidates its own ticket's plan-review attestation' is WITHDRAWN as incorrect. I inferred it from a single gate message ('stale-code: 4 dependency file(s) changed') without reading the currency/drift implementation, and my previous retraction was itself inadequate - it withdrew only the extrapolations while still calling the core claim 'sound and directly evidenced'. It was not: an error message naming changed files is not evidence for a general rule about what invalidates an attestation, and I did not establish what the drift check actually compares. I am deliberately NOT offering a replacement hypothesis. Nothing in this run should be read as an established fact about attestation currency. If this ever needs to be acted on, it goes through /rebar-debug for a proven, cited mechanism. Practically, closing 4329 needs only a current attestation, which requires re-running the review - no theory of the mechanism is required to do that."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787375290969454001,"uuid":"fc521716-f792-40ab-83a6-91760a9d0f98"}